nging from 636 to 3,390 sq ft, the development carries an estimated \nGDV of RM276 million. As of 31 December 2024, Isola KLCC had achieved a commendable take-up rate of 88%. \nA key milestone was reached on 12 February 2025 when the project obtained its CCC, with handover of units to \npurchasers already in progress, marking the successful completion of this premier high-rise development ahead of \nits earlier projected timeline.\nIsola KLCC--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOCR Opens Isola@KLCC Sales Gallery And Show Unit - OCR Group Berhad (https://ocrbhd.com/press-releases/ocr-opens-isolaklcc-sales-gallery-and-show-unit/)\nciteturn274search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9.5 years ago; Crawled: 2 weeks ago; 25 Apr, 2017 OCR Opens Isola@KLCC Sales Gallery And Show Unit ... KUALA LUMPUR: O&C Resources Bhd, a Bursa Malaysia Main Market Listed company, had on last Saturday unveiled the signature Sales Gallery and Show Unit of its latest luxury service residence project – Isola@KLCC at Jalan Yap Kwan Seng, a freehold project with a gross development value (GDV) of RM240mil targeted for completion by 2021.\n\nThe name “Isola” is derived from the Italian word meaning “Island”, reflected in the masterplan of Isola@KLCC, where each unit occupies a floor on its own.\nIt is a low­density development that offers only 140 units, ranging from one to three bedrooms, with build­ups of 636 to 3,390 sq ft.\n\nWith its masterful design and modern luxury, along with a fantastic city view, Isola@KLCC provides various facilities such as a business centre, resident lounge, sky pool, indoor gym and party suite, offering great convenience to promote a healthy work life balance.\n\nOCR managing director Billy Ong Kah Hoe said Isola@KLCC will have all the distinctive hallmarks of an OCR development – modern living, great location, superb connectivity and access to a widerange of amenities nearby.\n\n“This complements the unique selling points 