er]--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOCR Opens Isola@KLCC Sales Gallery And Show Unit @ Jalan Yap Kwan Seng - OCR Group Berhad (https://ocrbhd.com/press-releases/ocr-opens-isola-klcc-sales-gallery-and-show-unit-jalan-yap-kwan-seng-2/)\nciteturn274search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9.2 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; 24 Jul, 2017 OCR Opens Isola@KLCC Sales Gallery And Show Unit @ Jalan Yap Kwan SengKUALA LUMPUR, April 25 – O&C Resources Berhad, a Bursa Malaysia Main Market Listed company, had on last Saturday (22 April) unveiled the signature Sales Gallery and Show Unit of its latest luxury service residence project – Isola @ KLCC @ Jalan Yap Kwan Seng, a freehold project with a gross development value of RM240 million targeted for completion by 2021.\n\n24 Jul, 2017 OCR Opens Isola@KLCC Sales Gallery And Show Unit @ Jalan Yap Kwan Seng\n\nKUALA LUMPUR, April 25 – O&C Resources Berhad, a Bursa Malaysia Main Market Listed company, had on last Saturday (22 April) unveiled the signature Sales Gallery and Show Unit of its latest luxury service residence project – Isola @ KLCC @ Jalan Yap Kwan Seng, a freehold project with a gross development value of RM240 million targeted for completion by 2021. A host of activities and delectable food and drinks were prepared for visitors and their family who visited the gallery located at Jalan Liew Weng Chee today.\nIsola @ KLCC is strategically located along Jalan Yap Kwan Seng, compromises four residential blocks. The name “Isola” is derived from the Italian word meaning “Island”, reflected in the masterplan of Isola @ KLCC, where each unit occupies a floor on its own. It is a low-density development that owners only 140 units, ranging from one to three bedrooms, with build-ups of 636 to 3,390 sq ft. With its masterful design and modern luxury, along with a fantastic city view, Isola @ KLCC provides various facilities such as a business centre, resident lounge, sky pool, indoor gym and party suite, offering great convenience to promote a healthy work life balance.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nIsola @ KLCC - Condominium/Apartment for Sale - Kuala Lumpur (https://www.edgeprop.my/new-launches/project/isola-%40-klcc-53084)\nciteturn274search10 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; Completion: 2028 ... SEE UNIT TYPES AND PRICES ... Isola KLCC by OCR Group Berhad is a freehold serviced residence located in the heart of Kuala Lumpur, offering units ranging from 636 sqft to 3,390 sqft with layouts from 1 to 3 bedrooms. ...   * Sekolah Seni Malaysia Kuala Lumpur\n\n# Isola @ KLCC\n\nKLCC, Kuala Lumpur, 50450\n\nSEE ON MAP\n\nCompletion: 2028\n\nCondominium/Apartment\n\nStarting from\n\n## RM 1,149,800\n\nEst. Repayment RM 5,060/ mo\n\nCHECK YOUR ELIGIBILITY\n\nStudio - 2 Bed(s)\n\n0 - 2 Bath(s)\n\n- Sqft\n\nImage: Price per sqft 140 Total units\n\nSEE UNIT TYPES AND PRICES\n\n## About this property\n\nIsola KLCC by OCR Group Berhad is a freehold serviced residence located in the heart of Kuala Lumpur, offering units ranging from 636 sqft to 3,390 sqft with layouts from 1 to 3 bedrooms. Positioned near the iconic KLCC area, it provides residents with a prestigious address surrounded by the citys vibrant lifestyle, business, and leisure hubs. The development emphasizes exclusivity and modern living, making it an attractive choice for urban dwellers and investors seeking a prime location with strong value appreciation potential.\n\nResidents of Isola KLCC enjoy convenient access to nearby amenities such as shopping malls, fine dining, entertainment venues, and cultural attractions within Kuala Lumpur city center. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOCR Group launches first phase of Kyra Collection affordable housing project in Shah Alam | EdgeProp.my (https://api.edgeprop.my/content/1911926/ocr-group-launches-first-phase-kyra-collection-affordable-housing-project-shah-alam)\nciteturn274search11 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.6 years ago; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; Priya Devan / theedgemalaysia.com February 26, 2025 | Updated 1 year ago ... The statement also highlighted that the developer had obtained the certificate of completion and compliance for its Isola KLCC condominium development on Feb 12 and has started handing over the units to its buyers. ... In the statement, OCR group managing director Billy Ong Kah Hoe said, “The successful launch of Kyra and the completion of Isola KLCC reflect OCR’s versatility in delivering homes that cater to different market segments.\n\nThe first phase of the development called Residensi Akasia is part of the Rumah Selangoku affordable housing scheme and offers a total of 963 units spread across two towers. All units will have three bedrooms and three bathrooms with a built-up area of 1,023 sq ft. The unit selling price is RM288,000. Residensi Akasia has a gross development value of RM287 million.\n\nKyra Collection, as a whole, will be spread across 20.46 acres and will be developed in four phases with 2,892 apartment units in total and a retail component.\n\nThe statement also highlighted that the developer had obtained the certificate of completion and compliance for its Isola KLCC condominium development on Feb 12 and has started handing over the units to its buyers.\n\nIsola KLCC, which is situated on Jalan Yap Kwan Seng, comprises 140 units with one- to three-bedroom layouts and built-ups ranging from 636 to 3,390 sq ft. Units are priced from RM1.15 million. The freehold project has an estimated GDV of RM276 million and is 88% sold.\n\nIn the statement, OCR group managing director Billy Ong Kah Hoe said, “The successful launch of Kyra and the completion of Isola KLCC reflect OCR’s versatility in delivering homes that cater to different market segments.\n\n“We remain committed to providing Malaysians with well-designed, high-quality homes, whether through affordable housing projects or premium urban residences. With Kyra, we are supporting homeownership aspirations, and with Isola KLCC, we are enhancing city living for discerning buyers,” he added.\n\nAccording to the statement, the developer plans to launch a landed residential development called D’Templer Hilltop Residences in Rawang, Selangor, in 2Q2025."
